  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Rain returns Thursday as colder temperatures follow \nFriday into the weekend, with mountain snow and brisk conditions.\n\nShortwave ridging coupled with westerly downslope flow will\nallow for mild afternoons today and Wednesday. High temperatures\ntoday will be around 70. Wednesday will be a few degs cooler \ndue to more clouds and lighter SE winds. Very dry today with \nmarginal fire weather concerns. See Fire Weather section below. \n\nRain is expected to move in by early Thursday as low pressure\ncrosses the Appalachians and over to the Mid-Atlantic coast.\nThere weren't any significant changes seen at the sfc or at  \n500 mb compared to previous runs with the system expected to \nimpact the area Thursday into Friday.\n\nBehind this system, much colder air will follow on brisk NNW\nwinds with the Allegheny Mountains seeing their first \naccumulating snow of the season starting late Thu night and \ncontinuing through Fri evening. A few inches of accumulation are\nlikely falling roughly in a 24-hr period from 06Z Fri through\n06Z Sat. \n\nRemaining colder than normal Fri through the first half of next\nweek under brisk NNW flow between low pressure well offshore and\nstrong Canadian high pressure to our west.",
